A status is **terminal** only when its `name` is one of the following (case-insensitive, exact match):

- `Done`
- `Closed`
- `Resolved`
- `Cancelled` (or `Canceled`)
- `Won't Do` / `Won't Fix` / `Wontfix`
- `Duplicate`

Do **not** rely on `statusCategory == "done"` alone. Many JIRA workflows put deployment-pipeline statuses in the green category — e.g. `Deployed to Stage`, `Deployed`, `Released`, `Ready for Prod`, `In UAT`, `Verified`, `Awaiting Deploy`, `On Prod` — where the ticket has real follow-up work (prod rollout, verification, sign-off) still pending. Treating those as closed would silently lose local work.

When the status name is not on the allow-list, leave the bead open. If you are unsure whether a workflow-specific name (e.g. `Complete`, `Delivered`, `Fixed`) is really terminal in this project, **leave the bead open** — a human can close it later; a mistakenly-closed bead cannot be un-lost.
